5495-aa96-7aa335bd67c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495248 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186495279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495249 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186495214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495249 #edb/ref 1061 616168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495249 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c1f9c4d4-8e93-5221-9ae9-b9e48f28f0d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495249 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186495277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495276 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186495041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495276 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186495044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495276 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186495045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495276 #edb/ref 1031 "Finding Unit Prices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495276 #edb/ref 1033 2555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495276 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "cef7c109-a883-5959-842c-c3cb8202ae04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495277 #edb/ref 1064 "Now, suppose that installing a fence costs $\\[math]360$ per yard. What would be the unit price per foot?\n\nFirst, notice that there are $3$ feet in $1$ yard.  \n\nTo find the unit price per foot, we *divide* the price per yard by $3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n360 \\div 3 = 120\n$$\n\nTherefore, installing the fence costs $\\[/math]120$ per foot.\n\nIn reverse, if we know that installing a fence costs $\\[math]120$ per foot, to find the unit price per yard, we would need to *multiply* the price per foot by $3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n120 \\times 3 = 360\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495277 #edb/ref 1065 15094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495277 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "15c0e757-69bb-5bfd-a417-6de7c79fa333" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495277 #edb/ref 1067 "Unit Prices With Units Conversions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495279 #edb/ref 1064 "A **unit price** is the price of a single item. To compute a unit price, we divide the total cost of a group of items by the number of items in the group.\n\nFor example, suppose a store sells a pack of $3$ shirts for $\\[math]12.$ \n\nTo find the unit price, we divide the total cost by the number of shirts:\n\n$$\n12 \\div 3  = 4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit price is $\\[/math]4$ per shirt." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495279 #edb/ref 1065 3104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495279 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1e8ab0cc-4a5e-57ca-a168-f89d110ff113" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186495279 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517483 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517483 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518265 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517483 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517483 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517483 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186518299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517483 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517483 #edb/ref 1045 "Finding Unit Prices" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517483 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186518269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517483 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517483 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186495276 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517483 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "3d177d8b-58a3-5a2a-b0d6-cb5cc61ea34f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517533 #edb/ref 1080 "$$2.30$ per cup" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517533 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517533 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "18dfcd21-294b-55e4-b41f-375155c5f78f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517555 #edb/ref 1080 "$$3.65$ per quart" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517555 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517555 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "239c18ff-9dd1-57f6-8621-96f43e3689ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517560 #edb/ref 1080 "$$2.20$ per cup" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517560 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592