the lemonade costs $$2.25$ per cup." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518153 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518153 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68552" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518153 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518153 #edb/ref 1071 "At a convenience store, a $5$-pound canister of licorice candy costs $$11.20.$ What's the unit price per ounce?\n\nAssume that there are $16$ ounces in one pound." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518153 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "694684ae-3bf6-514c-9bb8-aef47c5c19c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518153 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we convert from pounds to ounces. There are $16$ ounces in each pound, so we multiply the number of pounds  by $16:$  \n\n$$\n5\\times 16=80\n$$\n\nSo, $5$ pounds is the same as $80$ ounces. Now, to find the unit price per ounce, we divide the total price by $80:$  \n\n$$\n11.20÷80=0.14\n$$\n\nTherefore, the licorice candy costs $$0.14$ per ounce." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518177 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518177 #edb/ref 1069 "q-354914" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518177 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518177 #edb/ref 1071 "Sarah bought $1$ ounce of almonds and paid $$0.75$ for it. What's the unit price per pound?\n\nAssume that there are $16$ ounces in one pound." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518177 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "924bf994-7977-5b78-af84-c2d13087032d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518177 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that there are $16$ ounces in each pound.  \n\nSince the price is $$0.75$ per ounce, to find the price per pound, we multiply by $16:$\n\n$$\n0.75\\times 16=12\n$$\n\nTherefore, the almonds cost $$12$ per pound." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518186 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518020 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518186 #edb/ref 1069 "q-354900" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518186 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518186 #edb/ref 1071 "Buying organic milk costs $$14.40$ per gallon. What's the unit price per quart?\n\nAssume that there are $4$ quarts in one gallon." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518186 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b6d906ea-b787-55f0-a205-6b6f9a337939" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518186 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that there are $4$ quarts in $1$ gallon. So, to find the unit price per quart, we divide the total price by $4:$\n\n$$\n14.40÷4=3.60\n$$\n\nTherefore, the milk costs $$3.60$ per quart." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518207 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518207 #edb/ref 1069 "q-354645" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518207 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518207 #edb/ref 1071 "Maria bought $1$ cup of olive oil and paid $$1.50$ for it. What's the unit price per gallon?\n\nAssume that there are $16$ cups in one gallon." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518207 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e1dac973-b461-5ce9-a7ae-b3034ec42db1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518207 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that there are $16$ cups in each gallon.  \n\nSince the price is $$1.50$ per cup, to find the price per gallon, we multiply by $16:$\n\n$$\n1.50\\times 16=24\n$$\n\nTherefore, the olive oil costs $$24$ per gallon." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518260 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518265 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518260 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "71aa048c-d524-5909-97e9-aeb85adb50c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518260 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186518207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518265 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518265 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "882bc0ea-f6bd-5db8-820e-a5ee597f7592" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518265 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186518186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518269 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1